"- Inner Bottle Wall\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A smooth, curved inner surface of a bottle, forming the inner boundary of the neck opening.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Deep, dark brown with subtle amber or coppery reflections along the rim and inner edge, appearing almost black in shadowed areas.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The inner wall curves inward from the rim to form a circular aperture; the visible portion is approximately 2-3 cm in diameter at the rim, tapering inward.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Glass, with a glossy, reflective finish.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of transparent glass with a dark tint, possibly due to the glass type or contents, exhibiting slight surface texture or residue.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One continuous inner wall surface.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Occupies the central interior space of the bottle neck, directly surrounding the central aperture.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - Curved inward concentrically, perpendicular to the bottle’s axis of symmetry.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - Attached to and seamlessly integrated with the glass rim and central aperture, forming a continuous inner structure.\n\n- Glass Rim\n    - Attribute 1 Type - The outermost circular edge of the bottle neck, defining the boundary of the opening.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Dark brown with a glossy sheen, reflecting light in warm amber or copper tones along its upper edge.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - Approximately 2-3 cm in diameter, with a slight thickness and beveled edge.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Glass, with a smooth, polished surface.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Made of dark-tinted glass, possibly borosilicate or soda-lime glass, with a uniform thickness and slight curvature.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One continuous rim.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Located at the very edge of the bottle neck, encircling the central aperture and inner wall.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - Horizontally oriented, forming a complete circular boundary.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - Connected to the inner bottle wall and central aperture, forming the outer boundary of the bottle’s opening.\n\n- Bottle Neck Opening\n    - Attribute 1 Type - The circular aperture formed by the inner bottle wall and glass rim, serving as the entry/exit point of the bottle.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Dark, deep brown with a blackish center, reflecting ambient light in warm amber tones along the rim.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - Approximately 2-3 cm in diameter, with a slightly tapered inner diameter toward the center.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Glass, with a smooth, reflective surface.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of the inner bottle wall and glass rim, forming a continuous circular opening.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One opening.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Positioned at the center of the image, surrounded by the inner bottle wall and glass rim.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - Circular and centered, with concentric curvature.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - Connected to the inner bottle wall and glass rim, forming the functional opening of the bottle.\n\n- Central Aperture\n    - Attribute 1 Type - The deepest, darkest circular void at the center of the bottle neck, where the bottle’s interior ends.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Deep black with no visible reflection, appearing as a void due to lack of light penetration.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - Approximately 1.5-2 cm in diameter, slightly smaller than the outer rim due to tapering.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Glass, with a non-reflective, dark interior surface.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of the innermost part of the bottle neck, possibly with a slight residue or texture.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One central aperture.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Located at the center of the bottle neck, surrounded by the inner bottle wall and glass rim.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - Circular, centered, and perpendicular to the bottle’s axis.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - Connected to the inner bottle wall and glass rim, forming the innermost part of the bottle’s opening."